/**
 * Withdraw the theme's `On this page` panel below the two-column breakpoint.
 *
 * Above that breakpoint the outline is a column of its own and costs a reader
 * nothing. Below it, the theme collapses the outline into a disclosure that sits
 * between the page's title and its first paragraph, so every page opened on a
 * phone begins with a control rather than with the page. The trail published
 * above the title already says where the reader is and how they arrived, which
 * is the question the panel was answering at that width; the outline itself is
 * reachable by reading the page it summarises.
 *
 * Rendering nothing rather than hiding it in CSS keeps the markup, the outline's
 * script, and the disclosure out of the page entirely instead of shipping them
 * to the readers least able to spend them. The outline in the right column is
 * untouched, so `tableOfContents` still governs which headings it lists.
 */
---
